    "reading": {
        "body": "Fifty models qualify for this collection under a four-billion-parameter-or-fewer cutoff, with a combined 144,040,448 downloads, led by Qwen3-0.6B at 22,741,013 downloads alone, roughly 16 percent of the category total.\n\nApache-2.0 is the dominant licence, covering 27 of the 50 models, more than half, followed by MIT at 6, Meta's llama3.2 licence at 3, Google's gemma licence at 3, and one model each under bigscience-bloom-rail-1.0 and an unspecified other licence, leaving 9 of the 50 models outside these six counted categories. The second and third most downloaded models, a testing checkpoint at 16,346,646 downloads and OpenAI's original gpt2 at 14,502,665, show that download counts in this category reflect a mix of production small models and legacy or utility repositories rather than production usage alone.\n\nMembership here is drawn strictly from safetensors metadata declaring a parameter count of four billion or fewer, and the data notes explicitly that models which do not publish a parameter count cannot appear in this collection regardless of their actual size, which means the 50 tracked here are a lower bound on how many qualifying small models actually exist.",
